The first length result is in: going from 4 to 10 document pages costs the compressed model nothing at seed 42. The seed-43 repeat and the 20-page and 40-passage cells are running. Nothing is needed from you.

## Done this wake
- **Both cells I was waiting on finished cleanly.**
  - The 300-question trial of the uncompressed model on 20-page documents passed in 17 minutes. The 19.5k-token prompt fits on one A100, so the two full 20-page runs (compressed and uncompressed) started after it.
  - The compressed reference model (seed 42) on 10-page documents ran all 1,500 questions with a judge verdict on every row. Its `<MEM>` slot total (slots = compressed pieces, 8 tokens each) matches the input audit exactly.
- **Length effect at 10 pages, seed 42.** This is the paired change, per question, in the gap between the compressed and uncompressed model, from 4 to 10 pages:

| input | `<MEM>` slots per question (median) | slots per page | compressed judge accuracy ↑ | uncompressed judge accuracy ↑ | gap (pt) ↑ |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 4 pages | 455 | ~114 | .610 | .809 | −19.9 |
| 10 pages | 1,125 | ~113 | .607 | .801 | −19.4 |

  - The change is +0.5 pt, 95% CI [−1.8, +2.7], sign test p .77, over 1,500 paired questions. Exact match (+1.6) and string match (+1.2) agree.
  - The CI sits inside ±3 pt, so there is no length loss at 10 pages so far. This is still one seed: it stays provisional until seed 43 agrees.
- **STATE.md** fixes the checker's points from the last wake:
  - Exact match had in fact been computed for the calculator check.
  - That the long-chunk loss "enters in stage 2" is an inference, not a measurement.
  - The training proposal is a recommendation to you, not something an arm tested.
- **`docs/longdoc_diagnosis.md`** now has the first length-curve table.

## Running now (4 new submissions, 35 of 70 cells used)
- Documents, 10 pages, seed 43: the repeat that decides the 10-page point.
- Documents, 20 pages, seed 42, compressed and uncompressed: about half done.
- Text, 40 passages, seed 42:
  - A 300-question trial is checking that the extra-passage option reaches text questions. I read the code first: it does.
  - The full compressed and uncompressed runs start after the trial.
  - The 10-passage results already recorded for this model (both seeds, same code) are the short-size baseline.

## Next
